  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Cytek’s operations started 2026 on a constructive note, driven by a strong U.S. instrument rebound and steady recurring revenue growth, signaling a normalization in its domestic market. Softer conditions in EMEA and APAC persisted, and wider net losses reflected elevated legal and consulting costs tied to patent litigation, which dampened profitability despite the top-line improvement.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management kept full-year revenue guidance unchanged, expressing confidence in the recovery trajectory and growing recurring base. The team is actively defending intellectual property in court, causing near-term cost spikes, but the company’s healthy cash position offers flexibility. No major shift in strategy occurred; the focus remains on expanding recurring revenue from the expanding installed base while navigating industry headwinds.",
